{"crc":"8dfaa9de","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that `QuerySet.none()` on combined queries (using `union()`, `intersection()`, or `difference()`) returns all results instead of an empty queryset. This happens because `none()` sets an `EmptyResultSet` on the query, but when the query has a combinator set (like `union`), the `EmptyResultSet` exception is caught and the combined queries are still executed.\n\nLet me examine the relevant code to find where this needs to be fixed.\n\nThe issue is in the `QuerySet.none()` method and how it interacts with combined queries. When `none()` is called on a combined queryset, it should return an empty queryset, but instead it returns all results from the combined queries.\n\nLet me look at the `none()` method in `QuerySet`:\n\n```python\ndef none(self):\n    clone = self._chain()\n    clone.query.set_empty()\n    return clone\n```\n\nAnd `set_empty()` in `Query`:\n\n```python\ndef set_empty(self):\n    self.where.add(NothingNode(), AND)\n```\n\nThe problem is that when a query has a combinator (like `union`), the `where` clause isn't used - instead, the combined queries are executed. So setting the where clause to `NothingNode` doesn't actually make the query return no results.\n\nThe fix should be in the `QuerySet.none()` method to handle combined queries properly. When a queryset has been combined with `union()`, `intersection()`, or `difference()`, calling `none()` should return an `EmptyQuerySet` or properly clear the combined queries.\n\nLet me search for the `none()` method and the `EmptyQuerySet` class:\n\n# path: django/db/models/query.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n=======\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        if clone.query.combinator:\n            clone.query.combined_queries = ()\n            clone.query.combinator = None\n        clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT2JN8ZCWH5MMQWB3NQ63RX","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT2JN8SBJ5J9A92D569JQW2"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786507787.1958258}
{"crc":"725f3d9c","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:513c02a07afb1be361128f4bbab169dac0991f47261e7ef9bcda138ebcc95429","instance":"01KZT2JYXV6ECQ9ZV7QW3XNMN3","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that `QuerySet.none()` on combined queries (using `union()`, `intersection()`, or `difference()`) returns all results instead of an empty queryset. This happens because `none()` sets an `EmptyResultSet` on the query, but when the query has a combinator set (like `union`), the `EmptyResultSet` exception is caught and the combined queries are still executed.\n\nLet me examine the relevant code to find where this needs to be fixed.\n\nThe issue is in the `QuerySet.none()` method and how it interacts with combined queries. When `none()` is called on a combined queryset, it should return an empty queryset, but instead it returns all results from the combined queries.\n\nLet me look at the `none()` method in `QuerySet`:\n\n```python\ndef none(self):\n    clone = self._chain()\n    clone.query.set_empty()\n    return clone\n```\n\nAnd `set_empty()` in `Query`:\n\n```python\ndef set_empty(self):\n    self.where.add(NothingNode(), AND)\n```\n\nThe problem is that when a query has a combinator (like `union`), the `where` clause isn't used - instead, the combined queries are executed. So setting the where clause to `NothingNode` doesn't actually make the query return no results.\n\nThe fix should be in the `QuerySet.none()` method to handle combined queries properly. When a queryset has been combined with `union()`, `intersection()`, or `difference()`, calling `none()` should return an `EmptyQuerySet` or properly clear the combined queries.\n\nLet me search for the `none()` method and the `EmptyQuerySet` class:\n\n# path: django/db/models/query.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n=======\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        if clone.query.combinator:\n            clone.query.combined_queries = ()\n            clone.query.combinator = None\n        clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786507787.1960058}
